subproblem.statement:
Let n, ℓ ∈ ℕ and Hⁿ := μHE[n] on ℝ^{n+ℓ}. Let A, A', O, Z ⊆ ℝ^{n+ℓ}, ϑ, ϑ' : ℝ^{n+ℓ} → ℝ, x ∈ ℝ^{n+ℓ} and P a linear subspace, and assume:
- A is Hⁿ-null-measurable;
- O is open with x ∈ O, and Hⁿ(Z) = 0;
- (A ∩ O) ∖ Z = (A' ∩ O) ∖ Z;
- ϑ(z) = ϑ'(z) for all z ∈ (A ∩ O) ∖ Z, and ϑ(x) = ϑ'(x).
If P is the approximate tangent space of A at x with respect to ϑ (Chapter03.HasWeightedApproximateTangentSpaceAt n A ϑ x P, Simon Def. 3.1.7), then P is the approximate tangent space of A' at x with respect to ϑ' (HasWeightedApproximateTangentSpaceAt n A' ϑ' x P).
